{"version":1,"slug":"compound-interest","topic":"What is compound interest?","level":"beginner","title":"How Compound Interest Grows","summary":"You will understand how earning interest on your interest makes money grow faster and faster over time.","scopeNote":null,"scenes":[{"id":"intro","kind":"intro","title":"What is compound interest?","segments":[{"id":"intro-0","narration":"Good question. What is compound interest? Let's figure it out together.","sig":"KNNOO_KzBb3EG2cWJ7ndUIXm2f9zJy_f","actions":[]},{"id":"intro-1","narration":"What if your money could earn its own money, and then that new money earned even more?","sig":"QLcwut6NWAcraaTprNu7XMQLn1DRLp-1","actions":[{"id":"hero","kind":"icon","cue":"What if your","text":"Money Growing Money","items":null,"icon":"piggy-bank","at":{"col":0,"row":1,"w":4,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]},{"id":"intro-2","narration":"Here's our plan. First, Interest on Interest. Then, The Snowball Effect. And finally, Time Is Your Superpower.","sig":"l_qSmTV95PPH156rv4p1c07cIAkj2Q3_","actions":[{"id":"agenda","kind":"timeline","cue":"Here's our plan","text":null,"items":["1: Interest on Interest","2: The Snowball Effect","3: Time Is Your Superpower"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":5,"row":1,"w":7,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]}]},{"id":"c1","kind":"chapter","title":"Interest on Interest","segments":[{"id":"c1-0","narration":"Imagine you put one hundred dollars into a savings account. The bank pays you ten percent interest each year as a thank you.","sig":"thRBC2Md__stLlEVeeKG6X_h7TOrxHL8","actions":[{"id":"bank","kind":"icon","cue":"put one hundred dollars","text":"Savings","items":null,"icon":"piggy-bank","at":{"col":1,"row":2,"w":2,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null},{"id":"start","kind":"number","cue":"one hundred dollars","text":"$100","items":["Start"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":4,"row":2,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"ink","expr":null},{"id":"rate","kind":"note","cue":"ten percent interest","text":"10% interest each year","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":4,"row":0,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"purple","expr":null}]},{"id":"c1-1","narration":"After the first year, you earn ten dollars, so now you have one hundred ten dollars.","sig":"NFE0T7FlFWOc_QZhvah5wz8e2PCXvXNo","actions":[{"id":"y1_arrow","kind":"arrow","cue":"earn ten dollars","text":"+ $10","items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":"start","to":"y1_total","target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"y1_total","kind":"number","cue":"one hundred ten","text":"$110","items":["Year 1"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":8,"row":2,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null}]},{"id":"c1-2","narration":"Here is the magic part. In year two, you earn ten percent on all one hundred ten dollars, not just your original hundred.","sig":"yGffJE6DzEGPYpqyRHCVvZzIUdZnpws1","actions":[{"id":"callout_y1","kind":"callout","cue":"magic part","text":"Interest on interest!","items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"y1_total","color":"orange","expr":null},{"id":"pulse_y1","kind":"pulse","cue":"all one hundred ten","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"y1_total","color":"orange","expr":null}]},{"id":"c1-3","narration":"That means you earn eleven dollars this time, growing your total even faster.","sig":"UxxCOyVQNj1MJ38A7lpfwKK2BmJ3MUJ2","actions":[{"id":"y2_note","kind":"note","cue":"eleven dollars this time","text":"Year 2: +$11 to $121","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":8,"row":4,"w":3,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"grow_y1","kind":"grow","cue":"growing your total","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"y1_total","color":"green","expr":"1.2"}]}]},{"id":"c2","kind":"chapter","title":"The Snowball Effect","segments":[{"id":"c2-0","narration":"Now that you know you earn interest on your interest, let's see what happens over a few years. Many people think you just add the same flat amount every year.","sig":"qxvg17ZGywU3eIliJ5bZGsWIC0McX81g","actions":[{"id":"wrong","kind":"box","cue":"same flat amount","text":"Same flat amount","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":0,"row":0,"w":4,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"red","expr":null}]},{"id":"c2-1","narration":"But that's not how it works! In year one you might earn ten dollars, then eleven dollars in year two, and twelve dollars and ten cents in year three.","sig":"K0vpX2hw-cwUbXlyLSfiCn5xO4DZBq66","actions":[{"id":"cross","kind":"cross_out","cue":"not how it works","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"wrong","color":"red","expr":null},{"id":"bars1","kind":"bars","cue":"year one","text":"Interest Earned","items":["Year 1: $10","Year 2: $11","Year 3: $12.10"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":5,"row":1,"w":6,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null}]},{"id":"c2-2","narration":"Just like a snowball rolling downhill, the amount of interest you earn gets bigger every single year.","sig":"hY_llaHfJGvlabzLyT5pfVqiaV-m971p","actions":[{"id":"right","kind":"box","cue":"gets bigger every","text":"Grows bigger each year","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":0,"row":3,"w":4,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"chk","kind":"check","cue":"gets bigger every","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"right","color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"p1","kind":"pulse","cue":"every single year","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"bars1","color":"green","expr":null}]}]},{"id":"c3","kind":"chapter","title":"Time Is Your Superpower","segments":[{"id":"c3-0","narration":"Because that snowball grows faster every year, the single biggest ingredient is time.","sig":"tPAsdD8x91ZFNKoCJcXDkqYa1oEui17F","actions":[{"id":"clock","kind":"icon","cue":"ingredient is time","text":"Start Early","items":null,"icon":"clock","at":{"col":7,"row":0,"w":2,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"blue","expr":null}]},{"id":"c3-1","narration":"Imagine putting away one hundred dollars at ten percent interest until age sixty-five. Starting at fifteen gives you over eleven thousand dollars, while waiting until twenty-five leaves you with four thousand five hundred.","sig":"s9pFjXmli9R6MCuhKgnnWkXByECPa1Gv","actions":[{"id":"age_bars","kind":"bars","cue":"Starting at fifteen","text":"At Age 65 ($100 at 10%)","items":["Start at 15: $11,700","Start at 25: $4,500"],"icon":null,"at":{"col":0,"row":1,"w":6,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null}]},{"id":"c3-2","narration":"Just ten extra years more than doubles your money, without adding another cent.","sig":"u7_dZ4YjsNozrPZrVkUaOFoN8pu8phFX","actions":[{"id":"call1","kind":"callout","cue":"ten extra years","text":"10 extra years!","items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"age_bars","color":"orange","expr":null},{"id":"pulse1","kind":"pulse","cue":"more than doubles","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"age_bars","color":"green","expr":null}]},{"id":"c3-3","narration":"So start early, be patient, and let compound interest do the heavy lifting for you.","sig":"lrz_wpbmr-NUlQyRAOK3EtwsVkhp6a-f","actions":[{"id":"patience_note","kind":"note","cue":"be patient","text":"Patience turns small savings into big results","items":null,"icon":null,"at":{"col":7,"row":3,"w":4,"h":2},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"purple","expr":null},{"id":"hl1","kind":"highlight","cue":"heavy lifting","text":null,"items":null,"icon":null,"at":null,"from":null,"to":null,"target":"patience_note","color":null,"expr":null}]}]},{"id":"recap","kind":"recap","title":"Recap","segments":[{"id":"recap-0","narration":"So remember: compound interest pays you interest on your interest, it grows faster every year like a snowball, and starting early gives time its full power. Got any questions about how it works?","sig":"-TV18-Im8OXWeS7PZtriUtK69dWiYSPX","actions":[{"id":"recap_list","kind":"list","cue":"compound interest pays","text":null,"items":["Earn interest on your interest","Growth speeds up every year","Start early for maximum time"],"icon":"circle-check","at":{"col":1,"row":1,"w":6,"h":4},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"green","expr":null},{"id":"recap_icon","kind":"icon","cue":"like a snowball","text":"Snowball Effect","items":null,"icon":"trending-up","at":{"col":8,"row":1,"w":3,"h":3},"from":null,"to":null,"target":null,"color":"orange","expr":null}]}]}],"quiz":[{"question":"What makes compound interest different from simple interest?","options":["You only earn on your starting amount","You earn interest on your past interest","The bank charges you a yearly fee","Your money stays the exact same"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Compound interest adds your earned interest to your balance, so you earn interest on a bigger amount each year.","chapter":1},{"question":"Why does compound interest feel like a snowball rolling downhill?","options":["It melts away if you wait","It adds the exact same amount yearly","The amount you earn grows bigger yearly","It only works during the winter"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Because your balance grows each year, the percentage you earn turns into a larger dollar amount every single year.","chapter":2},{"question":"What is the biggest ingredient for growing compound interest?","options":["Giving your money plenty of time","Checking your account every single day","Moving your money to different banks","Waiting until you are twenty-five"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Starting early gives your money more years to multiply, which makes a huge difference in your final total.","chapter":3}],"suggestions":["How inflation affects your savings","The Rule of Seventy-Two","How credit card debt compounds"],"models":{"lesson":"google/gemini-4-hydrogen","voice":"google/gemini-3.8-flash-tts"},"createdAt":"2026-11-17T17:39:24.266Z","audioBase":"/samples/compound-interest"}